439
00:23:44,092 --> 00:23:44,975
Chapter nine.

440
00:23:44,975 --> 00:23:48,684
How big is a matrix?

441
00:23:48,692 --> 00:23:51,139
A matrix has two natural sizes.

442
00:23:51,139 --> 00:23:55,218
The Frobenius norm treats it as a list of numbers:

443
00:23:55,218 --> 00:23:58,073
the root of the sum of squares.

444
00:23:58,073 --> 00:24:01,336
The spectral norm treats it as a map:

445
00:24:01,336 --> 00:24:05,415
the most it stretches any vector, the top singular value.

446
00:24:05,415 --> 00:24:10,717
The squared Frobenius norm is the trace of A transpose A, and the

447
00:24:10,717 --> 00:24:15,203
